          {
            "element": {
              "id": "coil_led_reset",
              "type": "coil_reset",
              "variable": "LED_Output",
              "row": 0,
              "col": 7
            },
            "hasWire": true
          }
        ]
      ],
      "branches": []
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "author": "ZPLC Team",
    "created": "2024-12-27",
    "modified": "2026-10-09",
    "iecStandard": "IEC 61131-3",
    "notes": [
      "A true 50% blinker with two TON timers and a SET/RESET output:",
      "1. Rung 1: while LED_Output is FALSE (NC contact passes power) OffTimer counts 500 ms.",
      "2. Rung 3: when OffTimer.Q is TRUE the SET coil turns LED_Output ON.",
      "3. Rung 1 opens (LED is ON), which resets OffTimer; rung 2 closes and OnTimer counts 500 ms.",
      "4. Rung 4: when OnTimer.Q is TRUE the RESET coil turns LED_Output OFF.",
      "5. Rung 2 opens, which resets OnTimer; rung 1 closes and the cycle repeats.",
      "Result: ON about 500 ms, OFF about 500 ms (each phase is 500 ms plus one 10 ms scan).",
      "",
      "Why two timers: with a single TON whose IN is the NC contact of its own output,",
      "the output rising opens the contact and resets the timer on the very next scan,",
      "so the LED is ON for ONE scan every 520 ms (a blip, not a blink).",
      "tests/blinky-visual.scenario.json checks both half periods, so a blip fails it."
    ]
  }
}
